  "frontier_coordinate": "R-135 restores the exact R-125 conditional future-variance rebate and identifies the complete-low R-123 trace excess as the live aggregate target. A scaled exact one-owner fixture proves that the R-134 scalar covariance envelope is unbounded below and cannot itself be the closure theorem. The R-087 three-channel spatial argument reruns directly on the uncentred R-088 sequential atom, with margins 1/15, 4/15, and 16/15 at alpha=2/5 and s=2/3; legal centring, the complete owner intertwiner, and the once-owned q_k^seq sum remain open. The exact self/sequential homotopy gives no termwise domination, and the accepted extracted-Z6 no-go does not refute the exact atom. Directed terminal refinements send the labelled last-block covariance to zero, so the production successor must use fixed-chart aggregate smoothing or a shell-weighted covariance and joint-spatial ledger rather than refinement-uniform last-block ellipticity. Positive finite-collar headroom, low and matching data, strict gap, absolute anchor, both A13 gates, OVERLAP_src, Nelson, removals, interacting measure, and Sector A remain open.",
